# Shell scripts are always LF, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. A shell script is the one file type that cannot survive it: bash
# reads the trailing \r as part of the command and fails with
# `$'\r': command not found`, which names neither the file nor the real cause.
# The founder's working copy is on Windows and deploy.sh is run from Git Bash
# there, so this is not hypothetical.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A repo-wide `* text=auto` would renormalise 700-odd HTML
# and JSON files in one commit, which is a large diff for no benefit — every
# other format here is read by tools that do not care.
*.sh text eol=lf
